## VLANs in short

A VLAN is a set of end stations and the switch ports connecting them, grouped logically (by department, project, etc.) rather than physically. A VLAN switch forwards on the Layer 2 header like a bridge (fast), but partitions the network into logical segments like a router — better administration, security, and multicast control. VLANs define broadcast domains: each is a distinct virtual bridge within the switch, and routers bound them because routers don't forward broadcasts.
